      { id: "ptm_200_01", categoryId: "sci_time", tier: 200, prompt: "According to Einstein's theory of relativity, what happens to time as you approach the speed of light?", answer: "Time slows down (time dilation) — a clock moving at high speed ticks slower relative to a stationary observer", acceptableAnswers: ["Time slows down", "Time dilation", "Time goes slower"], explanation: "Time dilation is not just theoretical — GPS satellites must correct for both special and general relativistic time effects to maintain accuracy." },
