      { id: "ptm_200_03", categoryId: "sci_time", tier: 200, prompt: "What effect does gravity have on time, according to general relativity?", answer: "Stronger gravity causes time to pass more slowly — clocks near massive objects tick slower than those in weaker gravitational fields", acceptableAnswers: ["Gravity slows time", "Stronger gravity means slower time", "Gravitational time dilation"], explanation: "A clock on Earth's surface runs slightly slower than one in orbit — this gravitational time dilation was directly measured by the Pound-Rebka experiment." },
